# NOTE: This file is NOT authoritative on this host.
#
# The telferwiki.com site is served from GitHub Pages behind a Cloudflare
# proxy. GitHub Pages does NOT honour Netlify's public/_redirects format, so
# the redirect declarations historically written here were silently IGNORED —
# which is why old-slug URLs returned hard 404s (e.g. /people/amy-nicole-telfer)
# and fed Google Search Console "Not found (404)" alerts.
#
# The AUTHORITATIVE redirect mechanism is repo-generated ALIAS PAGES:
#
#     scripts/generate-redirects.mjs
#
#   which runs in `postbuild` and writes dist/people/<from>/index.html stubs,
#   each carrying: <meta http-equiv="refresh"> + absolute <link rel="canonical">
#   + <meta name="robots" content="noindex">, pointing to the final LIVE page.
#   GitHub Pages serves these static files directly, so they work on this host.
#
# The integrity of that whole alias layer is enforced every deploy by:
#
#     scripts/check-redirect-health.mjs    (also in postbuild; fails the build
#                                           if any alias 404s, is relative, lacks
#                                           noindex, or is a multi-hop/dead link)
#
# Alias → destination list: scripts/redirect-log.json (auto-regenerated).
#
# Do NOT add redirect rules here expecting them to apply — the generator +
# health gate are the source of truth. Add legacy aliases to MANUAL_ALIASES
# in scripts/generate-redirects.mjs instead.
